WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.835
Most eyes and attention this

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.269
week were on the missile

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.504
that landed in Poland

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:05.572
just over the border

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:07.273
from Ukraine on Tuesday.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:08.074
But the United States

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.009
does not believe

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:11.544
that Russia fired that missile.

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:12.712
What we all should have been

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:13.413
paying attention

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:14.948
to was the devastating

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.916
aerial bombardment of Ukraine

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.752
that Moscow delivered this week.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:20.553
The British Ministry of Defense said

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:22.022
Tuesday saw likely

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.790
the largest number of strikes

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.292
that Russia has conducted in a single day

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.828
since the first week of the invasion.

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:29.996
One of the main targets

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:30.897
has been energy

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.032
infrastructure,

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:33.366
plunging swathes of Ukraine

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:34.601
into darkness.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:35.168
The capital,

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:36.936
Kiev, experienced both blackouts

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:38.972
and communication disruptions

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:41.007
All this as winter cold

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:43.076
and snow have arrived.

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:44.210
Let me bring in the panel

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.378
to talk about Ukraine,

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:46.946
and we will later get to China.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.148
I have two terrific guests

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:49.682
joining me in studio,

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:51.751
Richard Haass and Tim Naftali.

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:52.719
Richard is, of course,

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:53.820
the president of the Council

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.088
on Foreign Relations.

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:57.257
And Tim is a CNN presidential

00:00:57.257 --> 00:01:00.060
historian and teaches history at NYU.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:02.562
So that

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:03.630
bombardment just

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:03.963
you know,

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.698
this is part of the new general

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:08.535
who's been put in place in Russia

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.203
This is the guy who oversaw

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.237
the Syrian campaign.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.473
This is exactly what he did in Syria.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:14.407
It is brutal.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.075
I mean, he is

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:17.510
and they are going for

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.411
energy infrastructure

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.646
they're basically plunging

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:20.880
the civilian population

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.216
into cold and misery. Right.

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:24.617
Can Ukraine

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.886
just keep taking these body blows?

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:27.787
Look, you're exactly right.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:29.756
This is the Aleppo ization

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.124
of the Ukraine war.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:32.292
Russia can't compete,

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:32.792
if you will,

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.127
on the traditional battlefield.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:34.861
So they're saying

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:35.995
this is our battlefield.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:36.663
We are going to

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:37.430
so increase

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.531
the misery

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.566
that we are going to try

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:41.334
to get you to shout uncle

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.103
and to come to the negotiating table

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:44.671
and give us enough so we can claim

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.106
this was all worth it.

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.540
History suggests not.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:47.841
You know,

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:49.909
the history of mass bombing during World

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:50.343
War Two,

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:51.311
it tends to stiffen

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:53.713
the spine of civilian populations.

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:54.647
But we'll see.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:55.915
It's part of Putin's larger

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.650
strategy to play for time.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:58.685
He's hoping the new House

00:01:58.685 --> 00:01:59.552
of Representatives

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.020
here might give him a break,

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.389
is hoping Europeans get cold this winter.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.958
Maybe they'll lose some of their spirit

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.126
of backing Ukraine.

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:07.961
And obviously, he wants to break the back

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:09.195
back of the Ukrainian people.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:10.597
I don't think it will work,

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:12.932
but that right now is his strategy.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.467
Do you agree with that?

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.336
Oh, it's absolutely his strategy.

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:18.037
He is looking for weakness.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.906
He is looking for a lack of resolve

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.007
on the part of Europeans

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:22.142
and the United States.

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.843
And like all autocrats,

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.345
he underestimates democracy.

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:25.879
Says one thing

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:28.081
you can count on from an autocrat.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:30.116
They think we are weak

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:31.951
and they always get surprised

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.586
when we don't back down.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.822
So we have to do is project to them

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.524
a sense of unity and resolve,

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:39.826
which we have so far been able to do.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.695
We have actually remarkably so.

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:44.397
Europeans and the United States

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.466
have continued to tell Putin

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:47.400
and to send signals

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.168
to Putin

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.002
that we mean it

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:50.236
when we want to defend

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.404
Ukrainian sovereignty.

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:53.373
But it does highlight.

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:54.941
Ukraine is going to be

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:57.577
devastated I don't know

00:02:57.577 --> 00:02:58.878
whether you could even come up

00:02:58.878 --> 00:02:59.612
with a figure

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:00.346
that would describe

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.915
what the rebuilding of Ukraine

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:03.383
is going to cost at this stage.

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:04.584
It's incalculable.

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.019
It'll look,

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:08.054
they this polarization

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:10.089
and this is a modern society.

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:11.257
You and I have both spent time

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:12.625
there even recently.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.928
And you go down to downtown Kiev

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:15.662
and you could have been

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:16.930
in any city in modern

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:17.997
you know, any modern city

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.532
in Europe and contemporary Europe.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:21.568
The cost of this, the human cost order,

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:23.203
like a quarter of the population

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:24.637
more has been displaced.

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:27.407
The physical cost now

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:28.308
I spoke to a friend

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:29.943
the other day in Kiev.

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:31.644
I think she's in a 20 a

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.880
she on the 23rd floor of her building.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.014
The only way to get to her

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:36.249
apartment is to walk up

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:37.150
and down the stairs.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.152
Imagine what this is like for the elderly

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:41.221
and for four young children.

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:41.888
So this is you know,

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.756
this is a conscious strategy.

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:44.657
It is it is brutal.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:47.594
These are war crimes. On an hourly basis.

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:48.962
That is what we are

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.897
seeing in the cost of rebuilding Ukraine.

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:51.431
The years

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:52.498
it will take, the dollars

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:54.100
it will take will be enormous.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:54.400
To me,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.236
you had a really fascinating piece

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.237
in Foreign Affairs

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:58.404
in which you pointed out

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:01.474
that Putin is in a conference

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:03.710
with a bunch of Russian journalists.

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:07.146
In answer to to one of his favorite

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.148
foreign policy experts.

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:11.718
McAnuff, who's been on the show.

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:13.253
The guy asked him about the Cuban

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:15.955
Missile Crisis and what did he say?

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:19.425
Kind of asked Putin,

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.594
are you going to be like Khrushchev

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:23.930
accepting a retreat?

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.732
And Putin actually it was even better.

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:25.999
He said,

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:26.666
are you going to be like

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:28.268
Khrushchev and Khrushchev?

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:29.335
And Putin says,

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:31.537
you mean accept a retreat? No.

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:32.739
He characterized

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:34.607
what Khrushchev did as a retreat.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.876
And what's so important, I think, is that

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:39.345
there is a sense among American

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:40.613
and some European elites

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:41.881
that the Cuban missile crisis

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:43.349
ended peacefully

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:45.785
because of statesmanship. On both sides.

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:46.853
There is no doubt

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:48.588
that statesmanship mattered,

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:51.391
but the initial move towards an offramp

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:53.960
was from the Russian the Soviet side.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.428
The Russians were scared

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:56.629
And the reason they were scared

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:57.497
was that they were looking

00:04:57.497 --> 00:04:59.132
for some lack of resolve

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:00.333
on the part of John F Kennedy,

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.434
and they didn't see it.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:02.535
And when John F Kennedy

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:03.870
imposed a blockade

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.039
and stuck by it, Khrushchev realized,

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:07.473
I don't want war.

00:05:07.473 --> 00:05:09.075
I've got to find an off ramp.

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:10.710
So what I was trying to share

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.679
was don't look to history

00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:14.847
to give you a reason to go to Putin.

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:15.782
And give him an off ramp.

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:17.717
If anything, it's the opposite.

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:19.986
Don't give Putin up a sense

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:21.688
that you want to end this

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:22.855
because he's looking for that.

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:25.058
He's desperate for straws.

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:27.460
Force him to want an off ramp.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:28.695
The way that John F Kennedy

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:30.630
forced Khrushchev to seek an off ramp

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:31.998
from the Cuban Missile Crisis.

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:32.932
That's it would agree.

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:34.267
But I would actually say Khrushchev

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:35.768
probably acted under slightly

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:37.870
greater constraint than Putin is now.

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.872
There was a degree of institutions

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:40.740
in the Soviet Union need.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:41.808
It was sclerotic.

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:42.542
You had a degree

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:43.910
of collective leadership.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.478
We have a personalization

00:05:45.478 --> 00:05:47.313
and a de-institutionalization

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:48.247
of that country,

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.382
which makes it frightening

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:50.850
that one man has so much power.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:51.984
But do you agree with him?

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:52.885
Which I think is right,

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:53.453
which is

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:54.120
we shouldn't

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.222
be searching for off ramps for Putin.

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:58.324
We should be maintaining pressure.

00:05:58.324 --> 00:05:59.926
Let him search for the off ramp.

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:00.760
Absolutely.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:01.227
And, you know,

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:03.129
the situation is is far from being ripe

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:03.963
for diplomacy.

00:06:03.963 --> 00:06:05.098
Neither side right now

00:06:05.098 --> 00:06:07.800
is prepared to to accept half a loaf.

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:08.801
What we want to do

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:11.037
is create the conditions for diplomacy

00:06:11.037 --> 00:06:13.172
rather than go directly into diplomacy.

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:13.606
All right.

